WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.480
In Virginia, some people call a vulture a buzzard.

2
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.340
In Britain, a buzzard is a kind of hawk.

3
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:11.380
So which bird do they mean?

4
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.180
One common name can mean different birds in different places.

5
00:00:16.283 --> 00:00:19.723
Scientists fix this with one name for each kind of living thing.

6
00:00:20.583 --> 00:00:25.443
A species is a group of similar organisms that can mate in nature and have young

7
00:00:25.443 --> 00:00:26.643
that can also reproduce.

8
00:00:27.643 --> 00:00:31.403
This idea works for many organisms that reproduce with sex cells.

9
00:00:32.263 --> 00:00:37.143
It does not fit organisms that reproduce without sex, and some different species do

10
00:00:37.143 --> 00:00:38.443
sometimes mate in nature.

11
00:00:39.403 --> 00:00:41.663
Each species gets a two-part scientific name.

12
00:00:41.663 --> 00:00:42.633
For more information visit www .mooji .org

13
00:00:42.633 --> 00:00:47.493
The first word of the name is the genus, a small group of closely related species.

14
00:00:48.413 --> 00:00:51.093
The second word names one species in that genus.

15
00:00:51.913 --> 00:00:53.773
The turkey vulture is Cathartes aura.

16
00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:56.833
The black vulture is Coragyps atratus.

17
00:00:57.553 --> 00:00:59.273
The genus gets a capital letter.

18
00:01:00.113 --> 00:01:01.673
The second word is lowercase.

19
00:01:02.553 --> 00:01:07.013
A scientist in Japan who writes Cathartes aura means the same bird you see in

20
00:01:07.013 --> 00:01:08.013
Virginia.

21
00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:13.447
Scientists also sort each species into eight main levels, from most general to most

22
00:01:13.447 --> 00:01:18.787
specific. They are domain, kingdom, phylum, class, order, family, genus, and

23
00:01:18.787 --> 00:01:21.627
species. A domain is the largest group.

24
00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:24.927
There are three: Archaea, Bacteria, and Eukarya.

25
00:01:25.967 --> 00:01:27.567
Plants and animals are two kingdoms.

26
00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.050
Think of a mailing address.

27
00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:33.870
Country, state, city, and street each narrow the search.

28
00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.110
The levels of classification narrow it too.

29
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:41.170
Organisms that share more levels are grouped more closely.

30
00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:46.930
Scientists decide the groups by comparing body parts, what organisms do, and DNA.

31
00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:50.310
Names can still change when scientists learn more.

32
00:01:51.283 --> 00:01:53.483
A dichotomous key is a different tool.

33
00:01:54.343 --> 00:01:58.423
It names an organism from traits you can see, one two-choice step at a time.

34
00:01:59.283 --> 00:02:02.643
Its order alone does not show which organisms are related.

35
00:02:03.503 --> 00:02:06.343
So how do scientists know they mean the same living thing?

36
00:02:07.163 --> 00:02:11.463
They use its scientific name, shared in every country, and its place in the eight

37
00:02:11.463 --> 00:02:12.023
main levels.
